        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a160943c-1dd7-5b23-ac50-298981f10469",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Charon Gardens Wilderness Area, Wichita Mountains Wildlife Refuge, Medicine Park, Lawton, Comanche County, Oklahoma\n- Organizations: U.S. Fish & Wildlife Service\n- Topics: geography, administration, population\n\nFacts:\n- Charon Gardens Wilderness Area is part of the Wichita Mountains Wildlife Refuge in southwestern Oklahoma.\n- Charon Gardens Wilderness Area is managed by the U.S. Fish & Wildlife Service.\n- Charon Gardens Wilderness Area lies west of Medicine Park, Oklahoma, and north of Lawton, Oklahoma.\n- Charon Gardens Wilderness Area covers 5,723 acres in the western portion of the Wichita Mountains Wildlife Refuge.\n- Charon Gardens Wilderness Area is dominated by rugged granite mountains, oak forests, and mixed grass prairies.\n- Lawton is the county seat of Comanche County in Oklahoma.\n- According to the 2010 census, Lawton had a population of 96,867 and was the fifth-largest city in Oklahoma.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "770a3595-62c4-55b6-9926-4bab54df500a",
        "text": "Page: Charon Gardens Wilderness Area. Sentence: The Charon's Garden Wilderness Area is part of the Wichita Mountains Wildlife Refuge in southwestern Oklahoma and is managed by the US Fish & Wildlife Service.\nPage: Charon Gardens Wilderness Area. Sentence: It is located to the west of Medicine Park, Oklahoma and north of Lawton, Oklahoma.\nPage: Charon Gardens Wilderness Area. Sentence: The wilderness area, dominated by rugged granite mountains, oak forests, and mixed grass prairies, covers 5723 acre in the western portion of the Refuge.\nPage: Lawton, Oklahoma. Sentence: The city of Lawton is the county seat of Comanche County, in the State of Oklahoma.\nPage: Lawton, Oklahoma. Sentence: According to the 2010 census, Lawton's population was 96,867, making it the fifth-largest city in the state.",
